{"name":"Dusky Grouse","hex":"#8e969e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dusky grouse","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A species of forest-dwelling grouse native to the Rocky Mountains in North America, Dendragapus obscurus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dusky_grouse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dusky grouse","blocks":[{"text":"The dusky grouse is a species of forest-dwelling grouse native to the Rocky Mountains in North America. It is closely related to the sooty grouse, and the two were previously considered a single species, the blue grouse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Dendragapus_obscurus_USNPS.jpg/330px-Dendragapus_obscurus_USNPS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dusky_grouse","wikidata":"Q543345"},{"title":"Dusky","blocks":[{"text":"Dusky is an English electronic music duo from London consisting of Alfie Granger-Howell and Nick Harriman. Formed in 2011, they have released music on various records labels, before setting up their own label 17 Steps in July 2014 with the release of the Love Taking Over EP."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dusky","wikidata":"Q16249370"},{"title":"Grouse","blocks":[{"text":"Grouse are a group of birds from the order Galliformes, in the family Phasianidae. Grouse are presently assigned to the tribe Tetraonini, a classification supported by mitochondrial DNA sequence studies, and applied by the AviList, International Ornithological Congress, the American Ornithologists' Union, and others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Metsis_ehk_m%C3%B5tus_%28Tetrao_urogallus%29%2C_Euroopa_suurim_kanaline_2012.jpg/330px-Metsis_ehk_m%C3%B5tus_%28Tetrao_urogallus%29%2C_Euroopa_suurim_kanaline_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grouse","wikidata":"Q201240"}],"ima